From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NotAlexNoyle <alexnoyle@icloud.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 11:13:40 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] layout: the offscreen embedding repaints the content when a
 popup closes
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

cavekit-offscreen-rendering.md R7 / chrome-look R2. In Jihad's embedding a XUL popup has no window of its
own: jihad_offscreen_composite_popups draws every open popup over the content's frame. Hiding the popup's
widget dirties nothing in the content widget, so when nothing else repaints — a menu item that only runs
a command, such as about:addons' "Check for Updates" — the last frame stays on the card with the menu
still drawn on it (measured on the device 2026-10-25; a dismiss by a tap outside repainted by chance).
HidePopupCallback now invalidates the popup's root widget once the popup is out of the chain, under
JIHAD_OFFSCREEN only; a normal windowed build is unchanged.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 layout/xul/nsXULPopupManager.cpp | 16 ++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 16 insertions(+)

diff --git a/layout/xul/nsXULPopupManager.cpp b/layout/xul/nsXULPopupManager.cpp
index c427738167..65db40a235 100644
--- a/layout/xul/nsXULPopupManager.cpp
+++ b/layout/xul/nsXULPopupManager.cpp
@@ -1193,6 +1193,22 @@ nsXULPopupManager::HidePopupCallback(nsIContent* aPopup,
 
   nsWeakFrame weakFrame(aPopupFrame);
   aPopupFrame->HidePopup(aDeselectMenu, ePopupClosed);
+
+  // JIHAD (the offscreen embedding, JIHAD_OFFSCREEN): a popup is not a window of its own
+  // here — the embedder composites every open popup over the content's frame
+  // (jihad_offscreen_composite_popups, widget/PuppetWidget.cpp). Hiding the popup's widget
+  // dirties nothing in the content widget, so when nothing else repaints — a menu item
+  // that only runs a command — the last frame, popup and all, stays on screen (about:addons'
+  // tools menu after "Check for Updates", measured on the device 2026-10-25). Repaint the
+  // content once the popup is out of the chain, so the next frame carries no popup.
+  if (getenv("JIHAD_OFFSCREEN")) {
+    nsPresContext* pc = aPopupFrame->PresContext();
+    nsIWidget* root = pc ? pc->GetRootWidget() : nullptr;
+    if (root) {
+      LayoutDeviceIntRect b = root->GetBounds();
+      root->Invalidate(LayoutDeviceIntRect(0, 0, b.width, b.height));
+    }
+  }
   ENSURE_TRUE(weakFrame.IsAlive());
 
   // send the popuphidden event synchronously. This event has no default
